title: A tiny calculator: the ALU
mode: vhdl
chapter: Buses and numbers
check: behaves
---- intro
The heart of a processor is the **ALU** (arithmetic logic unit). It gets two numbers and an **operation** code, and gives the result of that operation:

| op | y |
|----|---|
| 00 | `a and b` |
| 01 | `a or b` |
| 10 | `a xor b` |
| 11 | `a + b` |

In hardware it works out all four at once, and a multiplexer keeps the one asked for. In VHDL that is one `with ... select`, with an expression in each case.
---- task
Make the 4-bit `y` the result of the operation `op` asks for (the sum wraps round in 4 bits).
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity alu4 is
  port(
    a  : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    b  : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    op : in  std_logic_vector(1 downto 0);
    y  : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end alu4;

architecture rtl of alu4 is
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity alu4 is
  port(
    a  : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    b  : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    op : in  std_logic_vector(1 downto 0);
    y  : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end alu4;

architecture rtl of alu4 is
begin
    with op select y <=
        a and b when "00",
        a or b  when "01",
        a xor b when "10",
        std_logic_vector(unsigned(a) + unsigned(b)) when others;
end rtl;
---- hint1
Use `with op select y <= ...`, one case per row of the table. The last can be `when others`.
---- hint2
The add case is `std_logic_vector(unsigned(a) + unsigned(b)) when others;`
---- solution
```
with op select y <=
    a and b when "00",
    a or b  when "01",
    a xor b when "10",
    std_logic_vector(unsigned(a) + unsigned(b)) when others;
```
---- done
Every instruction a processor runs, add, and, or, is the ALU with a different `op`. Make it 32 bits wide and give it a few more operations, and it is the real thing. Next: circuits that remember.
